             }
         }
 
-        if (!cacheEnsureSize(cache, size)) {
+        /*
+         * ARGON: a cache with no room is not a picture that cannot be drawn.
+         *
+         * This was `if (!cacheEnsureSize(...)) break;` - give up, hand a null
+         * Art back through artLock, and leave the caller to draw nothing or,
+         * as happened on 16 September 2026 in the middle of Maxim's game, to
+         * blit from address zero.  I called that null "the cache behaving as
+         * it should".  It is not, and he said so: "он так не должен".
+         *
+         * Everything below this line already knows what to do when the cache
+         * is full - ask the heap, borrow a big block from the arena, and in
+         * the last resort empty the cache and allocate anyway - and none of
+         * it was ever reached, because the first gate refused.  What
+         * cacheEnsureSize reports is whether the SWEEP could get the total
+         * down, and it cannot when the rest of the cache is locked: on the
+         * world map the interface art is on screen and held, and interface
+         * art is the one kind that cannot be used where it lies in flash,
+         * because the engine draws into it (see ag_art_store_ptr).
+         *
+         * So the sweep is still asked for - it is how the cache stays near
+         * its budget - and its answer no longer ends the attempt.  A block
+         * bigger than the whole cache is still refused here: that bound is
+         * what keeps one picture from spilling without limit into an arena
+         * that peaks at 5977 KB of 6000 during a map load.
+         */
+        if (size > cache->maxSize) {
             break;
         }
+        cacheEnsureSize(cache, size);
 
         bool allocated = false;
 
